{
  "name": "iris-lean",
  "description": "A Lean 4 formalization and port of the Iris higher-order concurrent separation logic framework, specifically implementing the MoSeL proof interface for mechanized reasoning. The project provides a specialized Iris Proof Mode (IPM) within Lean, utilizing custom tactics and type-class-driven automation to facilitate proofs in diverse separation logics. It includes fundamental algebraic abstractions such as Canonical Mixed Radical Algebras (CMRA) and Ordered Families of Equivalences (OFE) to support complex safety properties of concurrent programs.",
